{"contents": [{"parts": [{"text": "Three-quarter aerial-ish view from the south-west across the wide avenue, late afternoon, showing the whole block-long building and the covered street passing under it. Architectural visualization of a mid-rise mixed-use parking building in Jeonpo-dong, Busan, South Korea. Massing (follow the attached diagram): a long rectangular block about 125 m north-south and 45 m wide, 6 storeys (about 29 m). Ground floor is tall (7 m) and split into two parts with a narrow street passing under the upper floors; floors 2-5 are car parking wrapped in a perforated dark-grey metal and warm brick-tile (jeondol) screen facade; the 6th floor is a glazed sports/performance hall on the northern part with a rooftop plaza. Muted palette: charcoal, warm grey, beige brick. Realistic, natural light, no text, no logos, no watermarks."}, {"inline_data": {"mime_type": "image/png", "data": ""}}]}], "generationConfig": {"responseModalities": ["IMAGE"], "imageConfig": {"aspectRatio": "16:9"}}}